    "verdict": "`net = tr_M^{z=1} - h*delta_{w_0}` is an n = 3 fact, NOT a characterisation of the two functionals. At n = 4 the difference is nonzero on 11 of 24 basis elements with four distinct values, and the trace at z = 1 is not constant off w_0 either. Every conclusion drawn from the identity STANDS, because each is evaluated on Delta and Delta lives in H_3(q): eps(Delta) = tr_M^{z=1}(Delta) follows from Delta's SUPPORT; the phase is a transport within one family; the z-free floor is net(dC) = -h*y_(2,1)(1). What does not stand is the unscoped sentence, now corrected wherever it appears. Recorded rather than quietly patched: a sibling PR warned about generalising an n = 3 coincidence on this very bean, and I had done it. Also worth keeping: imposing the Markov property only at the top generator leaves the trace UNDERDETERMINED (rank 5 of 6 at n = 3)."
